An improbable but perfectly valid setup. However, atheist games also
have the restriction of no altars. As for holy water, either you
randomly find it or create it (if possible) with B?oRC. As for BUC
testing, you're stuck with ?oID, spell of identify and pet-BUC testing
before reaching Gehennom, where you can find a non-aligned altar,
which I think is impossible to destroy. In either case, the ideal role
for this restriction is the priest, which starts with holy water and
automatically knows the BUC of items.
Oh, and several roles have co-aligned or convertable altars on
quest levels which are not bones-eligible.

